  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "iloc_box_read",
    "file": "gpac/src/isomedia/box_code_meta.c",
    "description": "`iloc_box_read` allocates a `GF_ItemLocationEntry` with non-zeroing `gf_malloc` and immediately adds it to the box-owned `location_entries` list before initializing `location_entry->extent_entries`. If a subsequent `ISOM_DECREASE_SIZE` check fails, parse-error cleanup calls `iloc_entry_del`, which passes this indeterminate pointer to `gf_list_count`, causing the wild-address read at `list.c:642`. The entry must be zero-initialized, or `extent_entries` initialized before publishing the entry to the owning list, with failure-safe cleanup.",
    "conditions": "A malformed/truncated root `iloc` full box must declare at least one item while lacking enough bytes for that item's fields. In this PoC, size 0 makes the root box extend to the 16-byte input; version/flags consume four bytes, the field-size word is `0x2020`, and item_count is `0x2020` (8224). The first entry is allocated and linked, then the item-ID `ISOM_DECREASE_SIZE(ptr, 2)` fails because no payload remains. `gf_isom_box_parse_ex` deletes the partially parsed box, reaching the uninitialized `extent_entries` pointer and crashing."
  },
